2. Begins a transaction for atomicity
3. Builds an UPDATE statement with an IN clause containing placeholders for all doc_ids
4. Prepares and binds the statement with the actual doc_id values
5. Executes the update
6. Commits the transaction (or rolls back on error)
7. Returns true on success, false on failure

The function uses a single UPDATE statement with an IN clause for efficient batched updates, all wrapped in a transaction for data integrity.

