This implementation:
1. Connects to the SQLite database "test_db.sqlite"
2. Creates the Department and Employee tables if they don't exist
3. Performs INNER JOIN to get employees with departments
4. Performs LEFT JOIN to include all employees
5. Simulates RIGHT JOIN (SQLite doesn't natively support it) using LEFT JOIN with reversed table order
6. Simulates FULL JOIN (SQLite doesn't natively support it) using UNION of two LEFT JOINs
7. Returns all results in the JoinAnalysis struct

Note: SQLite has limited JOIN support compared to other databases, so RIGHT JOIN and FULL JOIN are simulated using equivalent SQL patterns.

